catalog.ai_prompt:
My Roblox game has a ModuleScript `DiscordCatalog` in ServerScriptService. Fill it in from my game, with the exact names the game uses:
- Catalog.Currencies: currencies, e.g. { "Coins", "Gems" }
- Catalog.Items: items and passes that can be a reward
- Catalog.Pets: pets with their rarity, e.g. { { Name = "Dragon", Rarity = "Legendary" } }
- Catalog.Eggs: the game's eggs, e.g. { { Name = "Basic Egg", Currency = "Coins", Price = 100, Pets = { Dog = 60, Cat = 40 } } }
- Catalog.Multipliers: the multiplier names my code reads with Live.GetMultiplier
- Catalog.SoldForRobux: currencies, items and pets players buy with Robux (directly or with a currency bought with Robux)
If the game already has modules with these lists, read them with require instead of copying the names. The module starts with local Catalog = {} and ends with return Catalog. Do not change the DiscordCodes script.
